On Tue, Jul 21, 2015 at 4:57 AM, Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>
wrote:

>
> You may have problems in redistributing existing cmavo between these new 4
> selmaho, though.
> E.g. {se'i}, {ri'e}, {zo'o} and {xo'o} by their semantics clearly belong
> to UI5=ROhA="interjection suffix"="categorizer".
>

"ri'e", yes. Not so sure about "zo'o" though. It's usually used as
standalone, and your grammar doesn't allow ROhA to stand by itself. And
doesn't "se'i" belong with "dai"?

I would accept having {fu'i} there too.
>

I don't really know what it is used for.


> But I'm not sure how {le'o}, {vu'e}, {ju'o} work as such suffixes. People
> almost never use {ju'o} as a modifier but on its own. So they'd rather
> belong to UI="interjection root" part.
>

"le'o" and "vu'e" seem to be what we might call "stances", they might go
with "ga'i". "ju'o" should go with "li'a", "la'a", they require a
proposition to relate to.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

